course: dictionary
lesson: 1153
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Brightness» is a good example. In «A light sensor measures brightness», it means how much light something gives off. In «Leo built a secret den... brightness turned down», it means a screen setting.
explain: Ask yourself what the sentence is about. Is it about light in science, a phone or tablet, or a happy face? The topic around the word points you to the right meaning. Then put your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
explain: Brightness can also describe colour and feelings. A bright red coat has strong colour. A cheerful person can have a lively brightness in their face or voice. It is the same word, but each time it has a different sense.
fact: Brightness is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say «the brightness», not «a brightness».
fact: «Brightness» means how much light something gives off or reflects. A bright lamp has high brightness.
fact: «Brightness» can also mean how strong and clear a colour is, or a cheerful quality in a face, voice or mood.
fact: On a phone or tablet, the brightness setting makes the screen lighter or darker.
fact: Phrases to know: «full brightness» means the highest level of light, and «turn down the brightness» means make the screen darker.
exercise: «A light sensor measures brightness, and code sets the screen brightness from it.» In the first part, what does brightness mean? | A cheerful, happy mood | The colour of the screen case | How loud a sound is | *How much light something gives off or reflects
exercise: Leo turned down the brightness on his tablet. What did this setting do? | It made the tablet heavier | It made the tablet louder | *It made the screen darker | It changed the colour of the case
exercise: Maya says, «Her brightness made the whole room smile.» What does brightness mean here? | How much light a lamp gives off | *A cheerful, lively quality in a person's face or mood | How strong a colour is on a wall | A screen setting on a phone
test: In «the brightness of the sun», what does brightness mean? | The strength of a colour in the sky | A screen setting that makes it darker | A warm, cheerful mood | *How much light the sun gives off
test: What does «full brightness» mean? | A colour that has faded | A sad or tired face | A quiet, gentle sound | *The highest level of light something can give off
exam: In «Leo built a secret den under his duvet: tablet, brightness turned down, sound off», what does brightness mean? | *A screen setting that makes it darker | The light of the Sun | How strong the duvet colour is | A cheerful face
